{
  "description": "Map values given defaults are unified to the type of the first key in sorted order",
  "spec": [
    "ext/typeexpr/README.md#optional-object-attributes",
    "spec.md#type-unification"
  ],
  "op": "eval",
  "features": [
    "functions",
    "type-expressions",
    "typed-values"
  ],
  "status": "disputed",
  "notes": "The README doesn't say that applying defaults unifies the values, and the spec's unification rules (spec.md#type-unification) would unify the object types of p, q, r and s attribute by attribute to strings, keeping \"01\" whatever the key order. The input also needs a map whose element type is the dynamic pseudo-type, which no value has in the spec. hashicorp/hcl adds the defaults to the map's values and unifies them in the sorted order of their keys (unifyAsMap in ext/typeexpr/defaults.go); because z is a map and the objects don't unify as a map, go-cty's UnifyUnsafe (cty/convert/unify.go) takes the first type in its preference order that the others convert to, unsafely if need be, which with sorted keys is p's type. The \"01\" of q, r and s converts to the number 1 on the way, and back to the string \"1\" when each attribute converts to its own type, while p keeps \"01\".",
  "variables": {
    "m": {
      "map": {
        "z": {
          "map": {
            "a": {
              "null": "dynamic"
            },
            "b": {
              "null": "dynamic"
            },
            "c": {
              "null": "dynamic"
            },
            "d": {
              "null": "dynamic"
            },
            "l": {
              "null": "dynamic"
            }
          },
          "element_type": "dynamic"
        }
      },
      "element_type": [
        "map",
        "dynamic"
      ]
    }
  },
  "functions": {
    "convert": {
      "extension": "convert-with-defaults"
    }
  },
  "expect": {
    "valid": true,
    "body": {
      "attributes": {
        "a": {
          "object": {
            "p": {
              "object": {
                "a": {
                  "string": "01"
                },
                "b": {
                  "number": "1"
                },
                "c": {
                  "number": "1"
                },
                "d": {
                  "number": "1"
                },
                "l": {
                  "element_type": "string",
                  "list": []
                }
              }
            },
            "q": {
